{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Avimelekh did not come near her.</b> It was necessary to state regarding Avimelekh that he did not come near her, more than regarding Pharaoh — because the conception of Yitzhak was close to the deed of Avimelekh." "<b>And YHWH said.</b> With alef-dalet." "<b>HaGoy also righteous will you kill.</b> Rearrange it: <b>הגם גוי צדיק, תהרוג</b>. And there are many verses similarly rearranged. Another interpretation: <b>הגוי גם צדיק</b> — גם is also an inclusive term, that is: if you kill me, who am called goy, you will also kill Avraham, for on account of his words I took her."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:04.144789237Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}